#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Arc Length of a Smooth Curve Using the Arc Length Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da1c47f5-5e7e-50ce-b14e-b9f3f3f757ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da1c47f5-5e7e-50ce-b14e-b9f3f3f757ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320054} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4fe866-71a8-5d45-8c02-73304c3706b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50520627-69a0-5672-92d6-61584ad60ba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-352870" :question/problem "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}$ for $x\\in [1,2].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}},$ $a=1,$ and $b=2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{6}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{8}(2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{4(2)^{2}}]-[\\frac{1}{8}(1)^{4}-\\frac{1}{4(1)^{2}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{16}-(-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083302 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Representation For an Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8851d870-2a19-5307-8c33-af68172b7885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081564} {:answer/id #uuid "930d8239-b612-5ec9-a778-197ab94cb52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 4}dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081565} {:answer/id #uuid "af92e866-31e2-5edd-b805-514b00a549b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{16x^{2} + 1}dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081566} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a99530-2687-5bcd-a1f4-d16e28d0d5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 1}dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081567} {:answer/id #uuid "694d36ea-c4f4-5041-b3ac-e7176a8e723a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{x^{4} + 1}dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081568}] :answer-field/id #uuid "db4fcd60-79e6-5854-b482-1b69ae6078d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081563} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f291e03-abb0-5fe4-a583-4a48393d5666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392737} {:answer/id #uuid "83980ef2-3253-5c8c-b7ac-9bf91e820d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392738} {:answer/id #uuid "16e21676-9e8e-5cda-891a-9e3a99ad370a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392739} {:answer/id #uuid "c65e70ed-792a-59d7-8500-3fca29572bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392740} {:answer/id #uuid "301b975b-e18b-51b6-9517-6f4e286dee3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "301b975b-e18b-51b6-9517-6f4e286dee3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392741} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca7ae0e-ab85-5150-9d28-8959d835e214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2c7c9a6-db2e-5889-8918-df15ae7908cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-51267" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb30925ffaca0ce59de7508e0f3710fbb26f3a80dfbd80b689e9ee5a4cf7d699.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}$ for $x\\in [-3,4],$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4},$ $a=-3,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2x}{4}=\\frac{x}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
